Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.88,0:00:22.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,今天的《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:00:20.88,0:00:22.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Today on How It's Made,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.36,0:00:28.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,卡车，公路巨兽诞生记
Dialogue: 1,0:00:25.36,0:00:28.00,Original,,0,0,0,,trucks, monster lorries come to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.92,0:00:33.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,创口贴，一年产量达40亿片
Dialogue: 1,0:00:29.92,0:00:33.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Plasters, four billion in just a single year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.76,0:00:35.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,那得有多少擦伤啊
Dialogue: 1,0:00:33.76,0:00:35.04,Original,,0,0,0,,That's a lot of grazes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.00,0:00:39.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,电脑电路板，为玩家、极客，也为所有普通人
Dialogue: 1,0:00:36.00,0:00:39.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Computer circuit boards, for gamers, geeks, and everyone in between.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.68,0:00:45.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有烈酒，从朗姆酒到白兰地，从伏特加到干邑
Dialogue: 1,0:00:41.68,0:00:45.28,Original,,0,0,0,,And spirits, from rum to brandy, vodka to cognac.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.16,0:00:46.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过先来看
Dialogue: 1,0:00:46.16,0:00:46.72,Original,,0,0,0,,But first,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.72,0:00:52.74,Translation,,0,0,0,,无论你心仪的车有8个、10个， 还是18个轮子
Dialogue: 1,0:00:48.72,0:00:52.74,Original,,0,0,0,,whether your rig of choice rides on 8, 10, or 18 wheels
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.74,0:00:56.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些公路巨兽都是货运行业的支柱
Dialogue: 1,0:00:52.74,0:00:56.80,Original,,0,0,0,,these beasts of the road are the backbone of the haulage industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.52,0:01:00.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,穿越国土，驶向欧洲乃至更远
Dialogue: 1,0:00:57.52,0:01:00.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Across our land and into Europe and beyond,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.40,0:01:03.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,从生菜到电脑，它们无所不运
Dialogue: 1,0:01:00.40,0:01:03.52,Original,,0,0,0,,they carry everything from lettuces to computers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.24,0:01:06.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎见证一辆卡车的诞生
Dialogue: 1,0:01:04.24,0:01:06.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the birth of a truck.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.80,0:01:14.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,制造这些巨型卡车需要极其复杂的工艺流程
Dialogue: 1,0:01:10.80,0:01:14.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Making these massive trucks requires highly complex procedures
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.64,0:01:17.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,因为零件又重又难操作
Dialogue: 1,0:01:14.64,0:01:17.28,Original,,0,0,0,,as the parts are heavy and tricky to handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.88,0:01:22.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,装配始于承重车架的制造
Dialogue: 1,0:01:18.88,0:01:22.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Assembly begins by fabrication of the bearing frame,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.56,0:01:26.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,将承载驾驶室、发动机和变速箱
Dialogue: 1,0:01:22.56,0:01:26.88,Original,,0,0,0,,the main part on which will rest the truck's cab, the motor, and the transmission.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.68,0:01:32.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,大梁有 7.5米和13米的规格
Dialogue: 1,0:01:27.68,0:01:32.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Tempered steel beams are assembled in lengths of 7.5 and 13 meters.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.32,0:01:47.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,底盘就像一套巨大的积木拼装而成
Dialogue: 1,0:01:44.32,0:01:47.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The chassis is constructed like a huge macaroni set.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.00,0:01:51.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,钢梁被逐一连接，用强力气动工具拧紧
Dialogue: 1,0:01:48.00,0:01:51.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The beams are attached together and tightened with powerful pneumatic tools.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.00,0:02:04.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,组装完成后，主底盘被送往下一个工区
Dialogue: 1,0:02:00.00,0:02:04.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Once assembled, the main chassis is transported to the next construction area.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.68,0:02:09.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在开始打造卡车的机械部分
Dialogue: 1,0:02:07.68,0:02:09.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the mechanics of the truck are created,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.08,0:02:12.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,包括差速器、车轴和底盘悬挂
Dialogue: 1,0:02:10.08,0:02:12.64,Original,,0,0,0,,with the differential, axle, and rig suspension.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.72,0:02:22.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后装好制动支架
Dialogue: 1,0:02:20.72,0:02:22.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The brake mounts are then put in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.86,0:02:34.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着安装轮毂
Dialogue: 1,0:02:32.86,0:02:34.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The wheel hubs are then attached.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.20,0:02:37.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,传动轴被插入其中
Dialogue: 1,0:02:35.20,0:02:37.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The transmission shaft is inserted,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.28,0:02:38.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,它将驱动车轮转动
Dialogue: 1,0:02:37.28,0:02:38.64,Original,,0,0,0,,which will power the driving wheels.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.80,0:02:51.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,组装好沉重的铸铁制动鼓， 完成后轮的安装
Dialogue: 1,0:02:46.80,0:02:51.68,Original,,0,0,0,,They finish the rear wheel assembly by mounting the heavy brake drum, made of cast iron.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.08,0:02:57.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,为便于安装，所有部件都倒置组装
Dialogue: 1,0:02:54.08,0:02:57.60,Original,,0,0,0,,To help with the mounting, everything is assembled upside down,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.24,0:03:02.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,由能吊起12吨重物的桥式起重机协助
Dialogue: 1,0:02:58.24,0:03:02.40,Original,,0,0,0,,with an overhead crane capable of lifting a 12,000 kilo load.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.12,0:03:05.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,将部件翻转正位
Dialogue: 1,0:03:03.12,0:03:05.44,Original,,0,0,0,,They then turn the part right side up.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.32,0:03:09.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,下一步是发动机的精细组装
Dialogue: 1,0:03:06.32,0:03:09.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Next step is the detailed construction of the engine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.84,0:03:14.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,变速箱被螺栓固定在黄色的发动机上
Dialogue: 1,0:03:11.84,0:03:14.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The transmission is bolted onto the motor, seen in yellow.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.32,0:03:19.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,在底盘前端安装离合器和变速箱
Dialogue: 1,0:03:16.32,0:03:19.84,Original,,0,0,0,,At the front end of the chassis, the clutch and the transmission are installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.44,0:03:23.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些卡车有6到10个轮子
Dialogue: 1,0:03:21.44,0:03:23.68,Original,,0,0,0,,These trucks have between six and ten wheels.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.88,0:03:28.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个轮胎加轮毂共重55公斤
Dialogue: 1,0:03:24.88,0:03:28.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Each tire and wheel together weighs 55 kilos.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.56,0:03:32.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,由于重量太大，车轮需借助升降装置安装
Dialogue: 1,0:03:28.56,0:03:32.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Because of the weight, the wheels are installed with the help of a lift mechanism.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.08,0:03:39.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这个螺栓器可同时拧紧所有车轮螺母
Dialogue: 1,0:03:36.08,0:03:39.92,Original,,0,0,0,,This bolt fastener allows tightening of all the wheel nuts at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.72,0:03:44.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,机械部分组装完成，接下来是驾驶室
Dialogue: 1,0:03:40.72,0:03:44.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The mechanical build is now complete, and it's onto the cab assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.96,0:03:46.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先进行喷漆
Dialogue: 1,0:03:44.96,0:03:46.24,Original,,0,0,0,,This begins with painting.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.16,0:03:58.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,驾驶室向前翻转，便于安装各类部件
Dialogue: 1,0:03:54.16,0:03:58.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The cab is flipped forward to help with the installation of various components.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.80,0:04:14.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是驾驶室内部
Dialogue: 1,0:04:12.80,0:04:14.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Now for the cab's interior.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.88,0:04:16.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先安装仪表台
Dialogue: 1,0:04:14.88,0:04:16.80,Original,,0,0,0,,They begin by installing the dashboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.52,0:04:22.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着连接所有线束、指示灯、车速表和踏板
Dialogue: 1,0:04:17.52,0:04:22.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Following this, they attach all the wires, indicators, speedometer, and the pedals.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.70,0:04:37.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后装好座椅，驾驶室完成后用螺栓固定到底盘上
Dialogue: 1,0:04:32.70,0:04:37.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The seats are then fixed, and with the cab completed, it's bolted onto the chassis.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.64,0:04:51.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后安装引擎盖、车灯、排气管和挡泥板
Dialogue: 1,0:04:46.64,0:04:51.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Lastly, the bonnet, lights, exhaust pipe, and mudguards are fitted.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.72,0:05:00.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,这辆卡车即将上路
Dialogue: 1,0:04:58.72,0:05:00.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The truck is now almost ready to hit the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.52,0:05:04.54,Translation,,0,0,0,,启动发动机，确认一切运行正常
Dialogue: 1,0:05:01.52,0:05:04.54,Original,,0,0,0,,They start it up and verify that everything is operating properly
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.04,0:05:07.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后就可以交付客户了
Dialogue: 1,0:05:05.04,0:05:07.52,Original,,0,0,0,,and now it's ready for delivery to the customer.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.84,0:05:19.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,组装这样一辆卡车需要100小时工时
Dialogue: 1,0:05:15.84,0:05:19.44,Original,,0,0,0,,It requires 100 hours of work to assemble a truck like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.40,0:05:22.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,尽管自重达5吨
Dialogue: 1,0:05:20.40,0:05:22.96,Original,,0,0,0,,And in spite of their 5,000 kilo weight,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.60,0:05:28.34,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些卡车最高时速也能轻松达到 120 公里每小时
Dialogue: 1,0:05:23.60,0:05:28.34,Original,,0,0,0,,these trucks can move along at top speeds of 120 kilometers an hour
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.86,0:05:32.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,并能运输重达28吨的货物
Dialogue: 1,0:05:28.86,0:05:32.00,Original,,0,0,0,,and transport loads of up to 28 tons.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.88,0:05:36.34,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们是公路上真正的劳模
Dialogue: 1,0:05:32.88,0:05:36.34,Original,,0,0,0,,They are the true workhorses of the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.24,0:05:44.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,手指割伤了？
Dialogue: 1,0:05:44.24,0:05:44.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Cut your finger?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.44,0:05:48.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,可以裹上厚厚的纱布，也可以贴一片创口贴
Dialogue: 1,0:05:45.44,0:05:48.96,Original,,0,0,0,,You can wrap it up in bulky gauze or you can apply a plaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.68,0:05:54.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,既然生活崇尚快速解决，创口贴总能胜出
Dialogue: 1,0:05:49.68,0:05:54.64,Original,,0,0,0,,And since we live in a society of quick fixes, the plaster wins out every time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.12,0:05:57.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,下次小家伙擦破膝盖时
Dialogue: 1,0:05:55.12,0:05:57.36,Original,,0,0,0,,So next time the little one grazes their knee,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.60,0:06:02.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,你就会知道那种叫创口贴的小绷带是怎么做成的
Dialogue: 1,0:05:57.60,0:06:02.40,Original,,0,0,0,,you'll know exactly what goes into making those stitches little bandages called plasters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.74,0:06:13.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,创口贴由多种材料制成，其中主要是ETS弹力布
Dialogue: 1,0:06:08.74,0:06:13.74,Original,,0,0,0,,Plasters are made of various materials, but the main one is called ETS,
Dialogue: 2,0:06:09.36,0:06:11.86,Annotation,,0,0,0,,ETS：单向弹力胶布
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.74,0:06:17.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种布只在单一方向有弹性
Dialogue: 1,0:06:13.74,0:06:17.52,Original,,0,0,0,,a fabric which is elastic in only one direction
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.68,0:06:19.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,并形成创口贴的粘合部分
Dialogue: 1,0:06:17.68,0:06:19.52,Original,,0,0,0,,and forms the adhesive part of the bandage.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.60,0:06:27.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这卷1800米长的布料能做出180万片创口贴
Dialogue: 1,0:06:21.60,0:06:27.84,Original,,0,0,0,,This 1,800 meter roll of fabric can make 1,800,000 plasters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.52,0:06:33.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,在布料的一面涂上薄薄一层胶水
Dialogue: 1,0:06:30.52,0:06:33.88,Original,,0,0,0,,A thin coating of glue is applied to one surface of the fabric
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.34,0:06:39.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,再送入烤箱加热到49摄氏度， 使胶层膨胀产生微孔
Dialogue: 1,0:06:34.34,0:06:39.68,Original,,0,0,0,,then it's heated to 49 degrees centigrade in an oven to puff it up, creating holes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.00,0:06:45.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后布料重新卷成300米一卷
Dialogue: 1,0:06:40.00,0:06:45.12,Original,,0,0,0,,In the glue coating, then the fabric is newly rolled up into 300 meter lengths.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.28,0:06:48.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,创口贴有不同尺寸
Dialogue: 1,0:06:47.28,0:06:48.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Bandages are of different sizes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.68,0:06:53.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,刀片把涂胶布卷切成不同宽度的条带
Dialogue: 1,0:06:49.68,0:06:53.12,Original,,0,0,0,,These blades cut the glued rolls into strips of varying widths.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.80,0:06:59.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些布卷随后堆放好，准备进入下一步
Dialogue: 1,0:06:56.80,0:06:59.52,Original,,0,0,0,,These rolls are then stacked, ready for the next step,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.08,0:07:02.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,粘贴那小块柔软的保护垫
Dialogue: 1,0:07:00.08,0:07:02.80,Original,,0,0,0,,application of the little cushioned protective pad.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.40,0:07:18.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器用打磨锋利的刀片切割布垫
Dialogue: 1,0:07:14.40,0:07:18.16,Original,,0,0,0,,A machine cuts the fabric pads with finely honed blades
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.40,0:07:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,刀片每6个月打磨一次
Dialogue: 1,0:07:18.40,0:07:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,that are sharpened every six months.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.28,0:07:28.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,柔软的布材被分成窄条
Dialogue: 1,0:07:25.28,0:07:28.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The cushioned fabric is separated into narrow strips,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.48,0:07:31.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,之后将粘到ETS弹力布上
Dialogue: 1,0:07:28.48,0:07:31.12,Original,,0,0,0,,which will later be glued to the ETS fabric.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.44,0:07:35.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些布条已准备好粘贴到创口贴上
Dialogue: 1,0:07:33.44,0:07:35.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The strips are now ready to be applied to the bandages.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.48,0:07:42.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,创口贴的各部分材料被展开
Dialogue: 1,0:07:40.48,0:07:42.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The bandage components are unrolled.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.52,0:07:47.54,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器将它们组装、切割并逐一包装
Dialogue: 1,0:07:43.52,0:07:47.54,Original,,0,0,0,,The machine assembles them, then cuts and individually wraps them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.96,0:08:01.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,贴上未印刷的白色包装纸, 用来保护创口贴
Dialogue: 1,0:07:56.96,0:08:01.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The unprinted white wrapping paper which protects the plasters. is applied.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.60,0:08:07.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着进入包装环节
Dialogue: 1,0:08:05.60,0:08:07.04,Original,,0,0,0,,And now they proceed to packaging,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.60,0:08:12.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,每分钟可包装300到1500片创口贴
Dialogue: 1,0:08:07.60,0:08:12.00,Original,,0,0,0,,where between 300 and 1,500 plasters are wrapped per minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.68,0:08:22.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,滚筒打出孔线，让创口贴之间易于分离
Dialogue: 1,0:08:17.68,0:08:22.56,Original,,0,0,0,,This roller perforates holes, which allows the plasters to be easily separated from one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.56,0:08:28.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,小型创口贴的制造方式不同
Dialogue: 1,0:08:26.56,0:08:28.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Small plasters are fabricated differently.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.08,0:08:34.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,布垫被放置在ETS的中央
Dialogue: 1,0:08:30.08,0:08:34.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The cushioned strip is positioned at the centre of the ETS fabric strip.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.30,0:08:44.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,布垫此时还未消毒
Dialogue: 1,0:08:42.30,0:08:44.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The cushioned pad isn't yet sterilised.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.12,0:08:45.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,还要稍等一会
Dialogue: 1,0:08:45.12,0:08:45.84,Original,,0,0,0,,That comes later.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.16,0:08:53.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,下一步是在创口贴两端
Dialogue: 1,0:08:50.16,0:08:53.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The next step is to apply two plastic paper protectors
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.68,0:08:55.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,贴上两片塑料保护纸，盖住涂胶的两端
Dialogue: 1,0:08:53.68,0:08:55.68,Original,,0,0,0,,over the glue-covered ends of the plaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.56,0:09:02.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,完成后，机械臂用吸力吸起创口贴
Dialogue: 1,0:08:58.56,0:09:02.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Once done, the plaster is drawn by suction with a robotic arm and
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.12,0:09:04.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,放入两层包装纸之间
Dialogue: 1,0:09:03.12,0:09:04.64,Original,,0,0,0,,placed between two wrapping papers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.40,0:09:09.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,慢镜头下，包装动作看得更清楚
Dialogue: 1,0:09:06.40,0:09:09.28,Original,,0,0,0,,In slow motion, we see the wrapping action better.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.92,0:09:13.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,全速运行时，每分钟可包装300片创口贴
Dialogue: 1,0:09:09.92,0:09:13.12,Original,,0,0,0,,At full speed, it can wrap 300 bandages a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.00,0:09:22.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,创口贴完美包装后从机器中出来
Dialogue: 1,0:09:20.00,0:09:22.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The bandages exit the machine perfectly wrapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.24,0:09:28.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,某些类型的创口贴还需经过
Dialogue: 1,0:09:26.24,0:09:28.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Certain types of plaster have to go through a
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.24,0:09:31.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,连续创口贴机打上透气孔
Dialogue: 1,0:09:28.24,0:09:31.92,Original,,0,0,0,,sequential bandage machine to have aeration holes pierced in them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.64,0:09:35.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些小孔让空气流通，有助于伤口愈合
Dialogue: 1,0:09:32.64,0:09:35.68,Original,,0,0,0,,These holes allow air to circulate and help promote healing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.56,0:09:40.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,创口贴现在准备好了
Dialogue: 1,0:09:38.56,0:09:40.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The plasters are now ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.12,0:09:46.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,有时会在创口贴包装上印刷说明文字
Dialogue: 1,0:09:43.12,0:09:46.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Sometimes instructions are printed onto the plaster wrappers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.96,0:09:49.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,两块聚合物印版从一系列滚筒上获取油墨
Dialogue: 1,0:09:46.96,0:09:49.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Two polymer plates receive ink from a series of rollers
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.24,0:09:52.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,以复制出所需图案
Dialogue: 1,0:09:50.24,0:09:52.48,Original,,0,0,0,,in order to reproduce the desired design.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.20,0:09:55.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,创口贴以极快的速度通过
Dialogue: 1,0:09:53.20,0:09:55.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The plasters pass through at incredibly high speeds.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.32,0:09:59.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,包装之前，它们最终经过消毒
Dialogue: 1,0:09:56.32,0:09:59.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Before being packaged, they're finally sterilised.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.00,0:10:01.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,一次消毒1万片
Dialogue: 1,0:10:00.00,0:10:01.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Ten thousand at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.48,0:10:07.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,创口贴被自动计数并送入滑道
Dialogue: 1,0:10:04.48,0:10:07.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The plasters are automatically counted and placed in a chute
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.60,0:10:09.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,落入包装盒中
Dialogue: 1,0:10:07.60,0:10:09.84,Original,,0,0,0,,and fall into the packaging box.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.52,0:10:20.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,开头那卷巨大的ETS布料
Dialogue: 1,0:10:17.52,0:10:20.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The large roll of ETS fabric seen at the beginning will
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.80,0:10:24.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,每年可生产近200万片创口贴
Dialogue: 1,0:10:20.80,0:10:24.56,Original,,0,0,0,,have produced nearly two million bandages each year.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.12,0:10:28.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂的年产量高达40亿片
Dialogue: 1,0:10:25.12,0:10:28.16,Original,,0,0,0,,This factory produces a staggering four billion
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.16,0:10:30.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,共65种不同款式
Dialogue: 1,0:10:28.16,0:10:30.64,Original,,0,0,0,,bandages in sixty-five different models.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.08,0:10:36.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来请看《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:10:34.08,0:10:36.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming up in how it's made
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.40,0:10:42.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,为玩家、极客，也给所有人打造的电脑电路板
Dialogue: 1,0:10:37.40,0:10:42.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Computer circuit boards from gamers, geeks and everyone in between.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.72,0:10:45.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,未来的电脑，就从这里开始
Dialogue: 1,0:10:42.72,0:10:45.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The computers of the future are here today.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.16,0:10:52.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有烈酒，从朗姆酒到白兰地，从伏特加到干邑，适合各种口味
Dialogue: 1,0:10:46.16,0:10:52.24,Original,,0,0,0,,And spirits, from rum to brandy, vodka to cognac, a tipple for every taste.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.96,0:10:53.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,广告之后见
Dialogue: 1,0:10:52.96,0:10:53.92,Original,,0,0,0,,See you after the break.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.68,0:11:07.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎回到《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:11:05.68,0:11:07.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.40,0:11:11.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后我们将看到烈酒，从朗姆酒到白兰地
Dialogue: 1,0:11:08.40,0:11:11.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Later we look at spirits, from rum to brandy,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.28,0:11:14.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,从伏特加到干邑，适合各种口味和场合
Dialogue: 1,0:11:11.28,0:11:14.48,Original,,0,0,0,,vodka to cognac, a tipple for every taste and occasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.12,0:11:15.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过先来看
Dialogue: 1,0:11:15.12,0:11:15.68,Original,,0,0,0,,But first,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.84,0:11:22.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,短短几年间，电路从一团乱麻的线缆
Dialogue: 1,0:11:17.84,0:11:22.08,Original,,0,0,0,,in just a few years, electronic circuits have shrunk from a tangle of wires
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.56,0:11:24.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,缩小到如今电脑电路板的尺寸
Dialogue: 1,0:11:22.56,0:11:24.88,Original,,0,0,0,,to the size of today's computer circuit board,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.92,0:11:27.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,而且还在一天天变小
Dialogue: 1,0:11:25.92,0:11:27.76,Original,,0,0,0,,and are getting smaller by the day.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.52,0:11:36.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,电脑技术的变化速度几乎超过地球上任何其他行业，来跟上脚步
Dialogue: 1,0:11:29.52,0:11:36.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Computer technology changes faster than just about any other industry on Earth, so keep up.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.04,0:11:47.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,电路板是电脑的一种部件
Dialogue: 1,0:11:41.04,0:11:47.36,Original,,0,0,0,,An electronic circuit board is a computer component
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.68,0:11:50.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,能渲染出惊艳逼真的画面
Dialogue: 1,0:11:47.68,0:11:50.24,Original,,0,0,0,,which can produce stunning and realistic scenes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.12,0:11:58.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这样的3D动画需艺术家和程序员借助图形处理器，耗时4个月才能完成
Dialogue: 1,0:11:51.12,0:11:58.00,Original,,0,0,0,,3D animation like this takes four months of work by artists and programmers with the aid of a graphic processor.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.20,0:12:03.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,印刷电路板好比一座建筑
Dialogue: 1,0:12:01.20,0:12:03.76,Original,,0,0,0,,A printed circuit board can be compared to a building,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.32,0:12:07.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻纤做的地板，铜线做的走廊
Dialogue: 1,0:12:04.32,0:12:07.28,Original,,0,0,0,,composed of fiberglass floors, copper passageways,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.68,0:12:10.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,以及连接各层的楼梯构成
Dialogue: 1,0:12:07.68,0:12:10.08,Original,,0,0,0,,and stairs that link the floors between them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.44,0:12:13.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,电路板采用两种技术组装
Dialogue: 1,0:12:11.44,0:12:13.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Cards are assembled with two technologies:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.00,0:12:16.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,表面贴装和直插元件
Dialogue: 1,0:12:14.00,0:12:16.48,Original,,0,0,0,,surface wiring and wiring through the card.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.20,0:12:20.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,元件放入孔中并焊接固定
Dialogue: 1,0:12:17.20,0:12:20.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The components are placed in the holes and soldered in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.24,0:12:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,用钢网将锡膏印刷到电路板上
Dialogue: 1,0:12:22.24,0:12:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,A stencil is used to apply soldering paste onto the card.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.40,0:12:28.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些锡膏将焊接表面元件
Dialogue: 1,0:12:26.40,0:12:28.72,Original,,0,0,0,,This paste will solder the surface components.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.28,0:12:32.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里把钢网放到印刷机上
Dialogue: 1,0:12:29.28,0:12:32.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Here, they place the stencil onto the printing unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.80,0:12:37.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,锡膏从这些孔漏下
Dialogue: 1,0:12:34.80,0:12:37.44,Original,,0,0,0,,It's through these holes that the soldering paste will run.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.88,0:12:44.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器将锡膏均匀铺开
Dialogue: 1,0:12:42.88,0:12:44.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The machine spreads the soldering paste,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.88,0:12:48.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,锡膏中含有锡铅合金等成分
Dialogue: 1,0:12:44.88,0:12:48.16,Original,,0,0,0,,which contains, among other elements, a tin lead alloy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.72,0:12:52.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,印刷刮刀开始工作
Dialogue: 1,0:12:50.72,0:12:52.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The printing blades go into action.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.84,0:12:59.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,锡膏穿过钢网孔，覆盖印刷电路板上的金属焊盘
Dialogue: 1,0:12:53.84,0:12:59.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The paste runs through the stencil holes and covers the metallic surfaces of the printed circuit board,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.52,0:13:01.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些位置将承载电流
Dialogue: 1,0:12:59.52,0:13:01.28,Original,,0,0,0,,which will establish the electrical current.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.68,0:13:13.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是未印刷电路板与印刷电路板的区别
Dialogue: 1,0:13:09.68,0:13:13.20,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the difference between an unprinted card and a printed one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.24,0:13:23.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来安装表面贴装元件
Dialogue: 1,0:13:20.24,0:13:23.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Next comes the installation of the surface wiring elements.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.84,0:13:26.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,由高速贴装机自动定位
Dialogue: 1,0:13:23.84,0:13:26.80,Original,,0,0,0,,They are automatically positioned by this rapid placement machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.60,0:13:33.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,每小时约安装3.6万个元件，相当于每秒10个
Dialogue: 1,0:13:27.60,0:13:33.12,Original,,0,0,0,,About thirty-six thousand components are installed per hour, making ten a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.72,0:13:39.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台极其精密的机器配备摄像系统
Dialogue: 1,0:13:36.72,0:13:39.36,Original,,0,0,0,,This incredibly sophisticated machine is equipped with a viewing camera
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.36,0:13:45.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,在安装前检查每个元件的对准和尺寸确保准确无误
Dialogue: 1,0:13:39.36,0:13:45.12,Original,,0,0,0,,which verifies the alignment and dimensions of each part before installation.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.20,0:13:58.86,Translation,,0,0,0,,另一台不带视觉校验的机器则补装间距小于0.5毫米的贴装点
Dialogue: 1,0:13:51.20,0:13:58.86,Original,,0,0,0,,A less precise machine then fixes parts where the space between two placement points is less than 0.5.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.00,0:14:10.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,电路板继续送向回流炉
Dialogue: 1,0:14:08.00,0:14:10.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The card continues on its way towards the oven,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.80,0:14:12.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,在那里完成一道关键工序
Dialogue: 1,0:14:10.80,0:14:12.80,Original,,0,0,0,,which accomplishes an essential operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.76,0:14:25.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,元件固定好后，电路板进入回流焊炉
Dialogue: 1,0:14:21.76,0:14:25.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Once the parts are secured, the card goes into a convection oven,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.92,0:14:28.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,高温将元件焊接在电路板上
Dialogue: 1,0:14:25.92,0:14:28.32,Original,,0,0,0,,where the heat will solder the parts to the card.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.44,0:14:37.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,各种电路接口被插入各自对应的孔中
Dialogue: 1,0:14:33.44,0:14:37.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Different circuit connectors are inserted into their respective holes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.92,0:14:39.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,这道工序需要灵巧的手法
Dialogue: 1,0:14:37.92,0:14:39.76,Original,,0,0,0,,This operation requires great dexterity.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.64,0:14:41.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,并由手工完成
Dialogue: 1,0:14:40.64,0:14:41.76,Original,,0,0,0,,and is completed by hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.24,0:15:01.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,金属焊点需要焊接到电路板上
Dialogue: 1,0:14:58.24,0:15:01.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The metallic placement points need to be soldered to the card.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.48,0:15:07.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,直插元件
Dialogue: 1,0:15:04.48,0:15:07.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The soldering of the circuit components through the card is done 
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.60,0:15:13.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,需要在240摄氏度的熔融锡铅合金浴中完成焊接
Dialogue: 1,0:15:07.60,0:15:13.28,Original,,0,0,0,,with a bath of molten tin-lead alloy at a temperature of 240 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.68,0:15:24.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在所有元件都已安装，可以进行初次电气测试
Dialogue: 1,0:15:19.68,0:15:24.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Now everything is installed, and an initial electrical test can be carried out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.96,0:15:27.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,电路板被放在带电的针床上
Dialogue: 1,0:15:24.96,0:15:27.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The card is placed on a bed of electrified pegs.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.56,0:15:31.50,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些探针接触电路板的连接点
Dialogue: 1,0:15:28.56,0:15:31.50,Original,,0,0,0,,These pegs make contact with the card's connecting points
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.50,0:15:35.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,从而检测电路板是否存在短路或断路
Dialogue: 1,0:15:31.50,0:15:35.60,Original,,0,0,0,,allowing them to check for short circuits or open circuits in the card.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.88,0:15:44.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后，电脑辅助的功能测试评估电路板的性能
Dialogue: 1,0:15:39.88,0:15:44.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Finally, a computer-aided operating test analyzes the card's performance.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.76,0:15:56.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家公司制造200种不同的电路板
Dialogue: 1,0:15:52.76,0:15:56.60,Original,,0,0,0,,This company fabricates 200 models of different circuit boards
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.60,0:15:59.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,每周产量约4000块
Dialogue: 1,0:15:56.60,0:15:59.92,Original,,0,0,0,,and produces about 4,000 cards each week.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.88,0:16:05.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,从玩家到极客，再到所有人，欢迎来到未来
Dialogue: 1,0:16:00.88,0:16:05.52,Original,,0,0,0,,From gamers to geeks and everyone in between, welcome to the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.76,0:16:18.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,世界顶级烈酒背后的秘密，归根结底就一个简单配方：
Dialogue: 1,0:16:12.76,0:16:18.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The secrets behind the world's finest alcoholic spirits all boil down to one simple recipe:
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.42,0:16:23.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,把谷物和水混合，然后发酵、蒸馏
Dialogue: 1,0:16:19.42,0:16:23.40,Original,,0,0,0,,mix grain and water, then ferment and distill,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.12,0:16:25.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,再加上几百年的传统工艺
Dialogue: 1,0:16:24.12,0:16:25.96,Original,,0,0,0,,add a few hundred years of tradition,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.20,0:16:30.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,你会明白为何酒精至今仍是全世界最受欢迎的杯中物
Dialogue: 1,0:16:26.20,0:16:30.92,Original,,0,0,0,,and you begin to understand why alcohol is still the world's favourite tipple.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.84,0:16:44.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,蒸馏的原理从古罗马开始就为人所知
Dialogue: 1,0:16:38.84,0:16:44.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The principle of distillation was known to ancient Romans, who mastered the process.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.84,0:16:48.94,Translation,,0,0,0,,中世纪时，蒸馏器首次从葡萄酒中制出酒精
Dialogue: 1,0:16:44.84,0:16:48.94,Original,,0,0,0,,In the Middle Ages, stills produced the first alcohols from wine.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.72,0:16:53.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,7世纪，蒸馏工艺得到改进
Dialogue: 1,0:16:49.72,0:16:53.40,Original,,0,0,0,,In the 7th century, the distillation process was improved,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.68,0:16:58.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,到了15世纪，工艺进一步完善
Dialogue: 1,0:16:54.68,0:16:58.12,Original,,0,0,0,,and by the 15th century, the process was further refined,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.60,0:17:01.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,才有了今天各种烈酒的生产
Dialogue: 1,0:16:58.60,0:17:01.40,Original,,0,0,0,,leading to the production of today's spirits,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.80,0:17:05.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,如白兰地、伏特加、朗姆酒、波本和威士忌
Dialogue: 1,0:17:01.80,0:17:05.80,Original,,0,0,0,,such as brandy, vodka, rum, bourbon, and whiskey.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.32,0:17:17.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,干玉米粒是酿造烈酒的主要谷物
Dialogue: 1,0:17:13.32,0:17:17.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Dried corn kernels is the main grain used in making spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.40,0:17:24.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家酿酒厂每天有几卡车玉米倾卸，共230吨
Dialogue: 1,0:17:18.40,0:17:24.24,Original,,0,0,0,,At this distillery, several truckloads empty out 230 tonnes every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.60,0:17:34.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米粒储存在24米高的储仓中，每座可容纳250吨
Dialogue: 1,0:17:27.60,0:17:34.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The kernels are stored in these 24 metre high silos, which can hold up to 250 tonnes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.52,0:17:39.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里是酿酒厂的中央控制室
Dialogue: 1,0:17:37.52,0:17:39.60,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the distillery control room,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.16,0:17:45.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,使用95%玉米酿造出中性酒精，
Dialogue: 1,0:17:40.16,0:17:45.20,Original,,0,0,0,,where they manage a recipe that's 95% corn and produces neutral alcohol
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.46,0:17:48.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,之后再加入其他谷物增添色泽与风味
Dialogue: 1,0:17:45.46,0:17:48.40,Original,,0,0,0,,to which other grains for colour and flavour will be added.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.84,0:17:52.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,第一步是碾磨谷物
Dialogue: 1,0:17:49.84,0:17:52.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The first step is the milling of the grain.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.48,0:17:56.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,约8吨玉米粉和1.8万升水
Dialogue: 1,0:17:52.48,0:17:56.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Some 8 tonnes of corn flour and 18,000 litres of water
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.96,0:18:01.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,被送入高压釜中蒸煮90分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:17:56.96,0:18:01.16,Original,,0,0,0,,are introduced into this autoclave and steam cooked for 90 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.36,0:18:05.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,酶将淀粉转化为糖
Dialogue: 1,0:18:02.36,0:18:05.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Enzymes transform starch into sugar.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.04,0:18:09.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着加入酵母，酵母把糖转化为酒精
Dialogue: 1,0:18:06.04,0:18:09.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Then they add the yeast, which convert sugar into alcohol.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.60,0:18:14.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,发酵在38摄氏度下持续60小时
Dialogue: 1,0:18:10.60,0:18:14.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Fermentation lasts 60 hours at 38 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.84,0:18:18.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,我们看到的气泡正是酵母活动产生的
Dialogue: 1,0:18:14.84,0:18:18.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The bubbling we see is created by the action of the yeasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.36,0:18:30.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,发酵开始至今已过去约24小时
Dialogue: 1,0:18:26.36,0:18:30.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Some 24 hours have now passed since the start of fermentation.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.56,0:18:41.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一阶段结束时，玉米油会浮到表面，呈明显的红色
Dialogue: 1,0:18:35.56,0:18:41.72,Original,,0,0,0,,When this stage is ended, corn oil will have come to the surface and is clearly visible by its reddish colour.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.44,0:18:50.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,发酵后的麦芽浆酒精含量为13%
Dialogue: 1,0:18:46.44,0:18:50.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The fermented mash has a 13% alcohol content.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.88,0:18:53.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在进入下一步——蒸馏
Dialogue: 1,0:18:50.88,0:18:53.76,Original,,0,0,0,,They now move on to the next step, distillation,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.24,0:18:56.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,蒸馏可让混合液中的蒸汽冷凝
Dialogue: 1,0:18:54.24,0:18:56.48,Original,,0,0,0,,which condenses the vapours of the mix.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.84,0:19:00.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,在这个三塔蒸馏系统中
Dialogue: 1,0:18:57.84,0:19:00.40,Original,,0,0,0,,It's in this three-column distillation system,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.40,0:19:03.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,麦芽糖浆在85.5 摄氏度下
Dialogue: 1,0:19:00.40,0:19:03.20,Original,,0,0,0,,at a temperature of 85.5 degrees,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.60,0:19:07.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,从蒸汽中分离出酒精
Dialogue: 1,0:19:03.60,0:19:07.84,Original,,0,0,0,,that the mash ferments and is distilled by steam to separate the alcohol.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.40,0:19:21.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,蒸馏期间，用这台旋转滚筒烘干酿酒中使用的谷物
Dialogue: 1,0:19:16.40,0:19:21.52,Original,,0,0,0,,During distillation, they dry the grains used in the recipe in this rotating drum.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.32,0:19:27.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,烘干后的产物叫酒糟，将用作动物饲料
Dialogue: 1,0:19:22.32,0:19:27.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The resulting product is called draff, and it will be used to make animal feed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.32,0:19:30.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,蒸馏至此结束
Dialogue: 1,0:19:28.32,0:19:30.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Distillation is now ended.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.46,0:19:36.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,为给某些金酒增添香气，他们会加入干柠檬皮、肉桂或香菜籽
Dialogue: 1,0:19:30.46,0:19:36.88,Original,,0,0,0,,To aromatise certain gins, they add dried lemon skins, some cinnamon, or coriander.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.22,0:19:43.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,朗姆酒和威士忌将装入橡木桶陈酿
Dialogue: 1,0:19:40.22,0:19:43.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Rum and whisky will be aged in oak barrels.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.52,0:19:53.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,陈酿期间，这些烈酒每年会因蒸发损失约3%的酒精含量
Dialogue: 1,0:19:47.52,0:19:53.76,Original,,0,0,0,,While ageing, these spirits will lose about 3% of their alcohol content annually through evaporation.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.48,0:19:56.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,同时，酒色会逐渐变深
Dialogue: 1,0:19:54.48,0:19:56.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Also, the colour gradually darkens.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.58,0:20:03.46,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在可以将酒液从木桶放出装入瓶中
Dialogue: 1,0:19:58.58,0:20:03.46,Original,,0,0,0,,They're now ready to draw out the liquid from the barrels and put it into bottles,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.46,0:20:06.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先必须检验烈酒的品质
Dialogue: 1,0:20:03.46,0:20:06.88,Original,,0,0,0,,but first they have to verify the quality of the spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.32,0:20:12.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,将标准产品与新产品进行对比
Dialogue: 1,0:20:09.32,0:20:12.28,Original,,0,0,0,,They compare the standard product with the new production.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.08,0:20:17.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一检验对确保成品质量至关重要
Dialogue: 1,0:20:13.08,0:20:17.48,Original,,0,0,0,,This test is highly important in order to assure the quality of the final product.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.40,0:20:24.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,灌装开始了
Dialogue: 1,0:20:23.40,0:20:24.92,Original,,0,0,0,,And so bottling begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.56,0:20:29.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里每分钟灌装140瓶淡朗姆酒
Dialogue: 1,0:20:25.56,0:20:29.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Here, 140 bottles of light rum are filled every minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.88,0:20:34.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,清洗干净的瓶子在传送带上不断循环
Dialogue: 1,0:20:31.88,0:20:34.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Clean bottles circulate continually on the conveyor,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.00,0:20:36.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,被送往灌装机
Dialogue: 1,0:20:35.00,0:20:36.44,Original,,0,0,0,,leading them to the filling machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.18,0:20:59.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,封盖机为瓶子盖上瓶盖并将其压紧在瓶口
Dialogue: 1,0:20:55.18,0:20:59.56,Original,,0,0,0,,A capper places caps on the bottles and crimps them onto the necks.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.24,0:21:03.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,封好并贴标的瓶子随后送往包装车间
Dialogue: 1,0:21:00.24,0:21:03.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The then sealed and labelled bottles head for the packaging department.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.36,0:21:18.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,另一台机器每分钟灌装120瓶加拿大威士忌
Dialogue: 1,0:21:13.36,0:21:18.56,Original,,0,0,0,,This other machine fills 120 bottles of Canadian whiskey every minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.40,0:21:30.06,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家酿酒厂生产约20种不同的烈酒
Dialogue: 1,0:21:26.40,0:21:30.06,Original,,0,0,0,,In this distillery, some 20 different spirits are produced.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.56,0:21:32.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,用3.4万吨玉米粒
Dialogue: 1,0:21:30.56,0:21:32.96,Original,,0,0,0,,With 34,000 tons of corn kernels,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.36,0:21:37.86,Translation,,0,0,0,,每年可生产4400万瓶烈酒
Dialogue: 1,0:21:33.36,0:21:37.86,Original,,0,0,0,,they produce 44 million bottles of spirits every year.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.48,0:21:38.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,干杯
Dialogue: 1,0:21:38.48,0:21:38.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Cheers.
